+Cost telemetry carries one of three states. `reported` is a figure the runtime
+stated directly (Claude's `total_cost_usd`). `derived` is a figure Citadel
+computed from a trusted observed token count and a bounded per-model rate table
+it owns, keyed strictly to the observed model, never the requested one --
+Codex, which never states a cost, gets one this way when its observed model has
+a listed rate. `unavailable` is neither: no trusted tokens, or a model with no
+listed rate. A derived figure is always distinguishable from a reported one by
+its cost source and is never presented as if the runtime had stated it.
